Weekly design tips and tricks from Canva
canva Weekly Tips
Tip 1

---------------------------------
Dazzle your audience with magic
---------------------------------

Designing a presentation is only half the fun. When presenting a Canva pres=
entation, there are many shortcuts to enhance your performance and keep you=
r audience engaged. While in presentation mode, try out the following:

<b>D for drumroll</b> - Build the tension before a big reveal with a drum r=
oll

<b>C for confetti</b> - Celebrate in style with a confetti shower on your f=
avorite slides

<b>Q for quiet</b> - Hush your audience to refocus their attention

<b>O for bubbles</b> - Add a touch of magic as bubbles rise to the top of y=
our slide

<b>B for blur</b> - Hide then reveal, combine with drum roll for big announ=
cements

<b>1 - 9 for count down timer</b> - Start a timer anywhere from 9 minutes t=
o 3 seconds.

Try it now=20
( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/N56jrjxtajclrFz56qumlZ8ZLt1PKVHyoU8DWXkqM=
-uSYS3EYGtgSWzLpcGe-vV2UB13BHf_nTaar7BXHulN0A/361/YcAQ4ttUR9qV75BsRIwn_w/t1=
2/7pJWS1CnpboOXyaq3IU7tChbk6gNPZjIpk1y22lSslg )

Tip 2

---------------------------------
Inspiration for your next presentation
---------------------------------

A little bit of movement in your presentation goes a long way. Simply hit A=
nimate in the top panel while in the editor to add a flutter of animation b=
etween your presentation slides. If you can=E2=80=99t see the Animate butto=
n, make sure you don=E2=80=99t have anything in your design selected. We ha=
ve lots of options to choose from to help keep your presentation fluid and =
eye-catching.

View presentations=20
( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/N56jrjxtajclrFz56qumlZ8ZLt1PKVHyoU8DWXkqM=
-uSYS3EYGtgSWzLpcGe-vV2UB13BHf_nTaar7BXHulN0A/361/YcAQ4ttUR9qV75BsRIwn_w/t1=
3/eV1rCcXTayhBrU5v8YicfD_O65Rzqwh3GXxcM8qbcpc )

Tip 3

---------------------------------
Sharing designs is simple
---------------------------------

Whatever you=E2=80=99ve created, be it a presentation or Instagram story, t=
here are many ways to share your design with others. You might want to get =
feedback as part of a collaborative project, or maybe you just want to show=
 off your designs to friends. Either way, it=E2=80=99s easy. Simply =E2=80=
=98share=E2=80=99 access to the design in the top right of the editor and a=
dd the recipient=E2=80=99s email address. Or copy and paste the link to sen=
d them. You can even give them edit access if you want their creative input=
 on your designs.

